# macOS Client implementation plan

Status: source integration into main authorized September11; developed on
`macos-client`, starting from main `bbbd307` / Client
`76979b90069916b593800277a24a31a03e0b778d`. Preserve Linux behavior. The remaining
interactive qualification gates below are not implied complete by this merge.

This records the original Mac Client port. The later
[Qt session integration](macos-qt-session.plan) supersedes its SDL window/input
details; consult that plan and HANDOFF for current implementation and acceptance
status. The Client minimum is15.0; the separately packaged Host minimum is26.7.

## Scope

September17 update: the operator authorized one SDK27-built Apple Silicon Client
package with a macOS15.0 minimum, preserving macOS27 features with runtime API
availability checks. At that checkpoint the Host remained27-only. See the current
Mac Client build runbook and `macos15-integration-review.md` for qualification;
the milestones below describe the initial macOS27 implementation.

Extend the existing Qt/SDL3 Client. Initial target is Apple Silicon, macOS 27
and SDK 27, built on the authorized dedicated development Mac. Reuse current
bookmarks, authentication, native Kyber transport, telemetry and session
lifecycle. No replacement protocol or temporary streaming client.

## Ordered gates

1. Reconstruct pinned private Qt 6.10.2, SDL3, OpenSSL, Opus and FFmpeg 9.0.1
   inputs. Document paths, versions, hashes and commands. Do not restore the
   inherited binary-prebuilts submodule. Preserve required dependency patches.
2. Qualify real profile-specific frames through VideoToolbox with hardware
   required. Record actual hardware status and decoded pixel format/range/
   matrix at 4K and 5120x2160. Include H.264/HEVC 8/10-bit 4:4:4 and Linux RGB
   identity. An API reporting codec support alone is not acceptance.
3. Compile the real Client with native transport. Repair macOS-only stale
   renderer/build APIs without restoring removed gamepad, pacer or networking
   subsystems. Use Metal/CoreVideo surfaces without CPU readback where exact
   format supports it; retain exact FFmpeg software fallback otherwise.
4. Make a real connection with video, CoreAudio output, keyboard, mouse,
   disconnect and responsive recovery. Qualify custom cursors and full-range
   presentation. Never substitute an easier chroma/depth/profile silently.
5. Validate toolbar interactions, fullscreen/window transitions, Retina pixel
   coordinates, display matching and multi-monitor behavior. Then qualify
   Wacom position/buttons/pressure; do not imply Linux raw-HID parity.
6. Produce a branded, signed/notarized self-contained Client app/package, no
   autostart. Retain exact source/dependency provenance and independent package
   checks. User acceptance precedes merge.

## Risk boundaries

- Existing VideoToolbox/Metal sources are unqualified starting points, not
  evidence of working 4:4:4 or RGB identity support.
- Hardware availability must be runtime-tested, not inferred from model names.
- Preserve the working macOS Host and its permissions; no TCC database edits.
- Do not use the read-only PCoIP reference Mac or clean deployment Mac.
- Do not install candidates on End-User machines without explicit permission.
- Stop for genuinely missing authorization/credentials or a human-only test,
  not for intermediate implementation steps.

## Qualification checkpoint — September 10

Pinned private build inputs and the real Client compile successfully. The
first self-contained signed/notarized DMG passed dependency closure, executable
version, signature, staple and Gatekeeper checks. A later package version gate
caught retained qmake subprojects using older source; recursive regeneration
is now mandatory. HANDOFF records the exact current candidate, not this plan.

Hardware-required decode passes HEVC10 4:4:4 full-range at4K and5120x2160,
and smaller Linux identity fixtures. H.2648/10 4:4:4 correctly takes exact
software GBR fallback on the tested Apple Silicon. Production Metal math
passes630 GPU checks covering biplanar/triplanar, identity and neutral YCbCr
ramps. These are not exhaustive color-management or display-panel tests.

First real Client-to-Linux-Host session:3840x1620 HEVC10 4:4:4 identity,
hardware P410 decode/Metal, CoreAudio initialized,4224 video frames, no receive
or FEC loss, approximately60FPS and clean termination. This was a mostly
static login screen, no input events sent, and not an audio listening test.
It exposed the Wayland-only tablet-cursor helper being invoked on Cocoa;
the driver gate now prevents this. Existing video-master audio correction is
also enabled for macOS rather than silently excluded by a Linux-only guard.
The shared audio-controller suite passes11 checks on the Mac.

September11: installed signed .95 now polls the Linux Host successfully after
user Local Network authorization. Packaged CLI streaming also passes hardware
HEVC10 4:4:4 identity/Metal with CoreAudio initialized, zero receive/FEC or
render-queue drops in a bounded~40second GDM sample. The test was stopped during
a newly announced desktop handoff; that handoff is not yet qualified. No
automated input was injected and audible output has not been confirmed.

Packaged desktop reconnect then passed a two-minute sample:7344frames,
59.76renderedFPS, zero receive/FEC and frame-queue drops, clean signal shutdown.
Automated AppleScript Quit returned cancellation, so normal human Quit remains
an explicit gate rather than inferred from signal cleanup.

Still required: Mac Host session when available,
human video/audio and pointer/keyboard/toolbar interaction, Retina and multiple
displays, prolonged moving-content A/V sync. macOS normalized SDL3 pen input
has not been wired/qualified yet; do not claim Wacom pressure or raw-HID parity.
Do not implement speculative pen work before the ordinary interactive Client
is accepted. Existing development-mac Host session must not be interrupted for testing.
